 "structural_change": "DRIVE-S81-LEPMU r6e (n32 gates FAIL: clock_rule spread, a keep_modules, h GRT ovf 2): wide-bus repartition, 0 added cycles (twin of DRIVE-S81-LEP r5e): the 10 RX landing SRAMs move into ONE column beside the E face (x 475.2, y 43.2+43.2k, orient MY so rd_out faces the ri pins); n32 gate had RX banks in two N rows across the width -> macro->reg rtq -233/-275 ps at placement (SRAM q -> E-face ri / N-face ml_wd up to ~500 um). RX read bus now stays in an E strip whose top end meets the N-face ml pins; TX columns unchanged (x 43.2 / 259.2, 86.4 pitch). Outline 475.2x561.6 -> 561.6x518.4 (W 2318/518.4 = 4.5/um, E 2362/518.4 = 4.6/um, N ml 2211/561.6 = 3.9/um, S host 705/561.6). Clock: NO km split, one TritonCTS tree (n32 gate km K8: a TT/FF spread 121.1/110.6, h 83.2/81.7; LEPNH 10-20: K8 unequal cluster depths 4..6 under a blind 8-sink top tree; pre-native one-tree lepnh 40.2/36.8). Same RTL (6cb5f3eff NATIVE32=1 incl LOCAL_WA, RX_SRAM=1, IN_PIPE=1), ports, cycles, SDC.",
